  {
    "description": "Default fixed background workflow for every new chat video, including a single short clip and a finished video longer than one model clip. Default to one finished work. For several user-requested works, first prepare_video_works with the concrete count and use each returned work_id once. This tool starts one finished work per invocation; clips and gateway concurrency never add works. Reuse work_id when continuing, correcting or retrying the same finished work. Its durable claim survives new tool-call ids and restarts; an existing work returns original task coordinates without a new generation POST. A new actual human request can prepare independent work even with the same prompt, plan or shots, and an earlier unknown task cannot block it. Natural-language phrasing and inferred work totals are not permission gates. pending_work_ids identifies concrete prepared works still available to start; start only those still requested by the user, without waiting for earlier jobs. If the user reduces the count, leave unwanted prepared works unstarted; never generate merely to empty this list. remaining_works counts that list, not a user allowance. Query or resume accepted and unknown original projects instead of generating again. For a simple single-clip brief without an explicit duration, call this tool directly with prompt and any requested model or references; omit total_duration_seconds so the Host resolves actual defaults in one call. Do not load directing skills, write a long storyboard or call list_video_models first for that simple case. For explicit timing or complex plans, read list_video_models for actual controls; never discover support by paid retries or silently replace an explicitly named model. Use the yunshu-video-director skill for story, character/reference continuity, dialogue and subtitles, then call this native workflow; do not write polling, download or assembly scripts or manually repeat generate_video for each visual cut. One paid clip can contain several camera beats. For requests such as a 40-second video, plan the fewest supported clips (for a 15-second limit: 15+15+10, or three 15-second clips trimmed to 40), generate independent clips with gateway-approved bounded parallelism using the signed-in account, then normalize, trim, and join them in timeline order. Without a valid gateway declaration, concurrency defaults to four clips. Respect verified pool capacity and any lower local or gateway ceiling. The API owns shared account capacity. Do not launch a separate agent or generation-tool call for every clip. For a catalog with H3 single clips limited to 4–15 seconds, 60 seconds means four 15-second clips, never one 30-second clip. All local tools and every request are checked before billing. Returns a background job_id and durable project_id; read job_output at measured intervals for queued/generating progress and call present on the completed final_path. A busy response without an accepted task id is unknown, not confirmed queue admission. Use job_kill when the user stops; accepted provider tasks may continue billing. A query deadline retains task ids for explicit resume, never a fresh submission. Never claim completion before the job reports a saved final_path. If a current user-supplied chat attachment is outside the workspace, first copy that read-authorized attachment into this workspace with the existing file tools, then pass the copied path; do not copy unrelated files.结合完整对话理解创作意图，不要求用户使用固定句式或反复重述数量。未指定数量默认一条；用户明确需要几条成片，就先用 prepare_video_works 准备对应数量，再逐个使用返回的 work_id 生成。单条简单请求可以直接生成，Host 自动准备一个默认作品编号。作品编号用于同一成片的防重复，不是从用户措辞推算的权限额度。普通确认、修改参数和继续同一作品时复用已有 work_id；尚未提交时可以纠正参数，已提交或结果未知时只查询、恢复原任务，不通过换工具调用或重新准备编号再生成。台词、字幕和故事里的疑问或否定不代表取消。准备同一请求会返回原作品清单，不增加版本；若已准备清单后，用户在真实问题回答中明确增加数量，先核对已有清单，再用 append_video_works 追加缺少的条数（已有一条改为总共三条时追加两条），保留原 work_id 和未知任务。同一回答重复追加不会再次加片，不能把普通确认、查询或重试当作追加指令。非 H3 报价选择只批准当前一件作品，追加作品分别核对实际报价；用户另行发起独立新请求时可以准备新的清单，即使提示词或计划相同，也不受旧任务等待或未知影响。清单中的待办不是必须执行的订单；用户减少数量时只启动其仍要求的作品，未启动的多余编号可以保留，不能为了清空清单生成。不要为了填满并发、质量评价或修改计划自动增加收费作品。是否另做仍不明确时只简短确认，不把正常对话说成平台拒绝。",
    "name": "generate_video_project",
    "parameters": {
      "properties": {
        "audio": {
          "description": "Optional requested audio state from list_video_models, not a capability probe. Sent as a switch only when the chosen model declares one; fixed native audio accepts only its declared state. No switch does not mean silent output; an undeclared audio state remains unknown. Do not blindly send true, and do not promise speech, lip-sync, subtitles or silence without checking the media.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
